# No filler disclaimers

The notepad and the parrot sell coming back. Do not add hedge lines to that copy.

Never write lines like these into the notepad, parrot bubbles, menu, or other pitch copy:

- "I can't promise the next one wins."
- "Past results do not promise the next ticket."
- "Last week does not promise this one."
- "21+. Only what you can lose. 1-800-GAMBLER." used as a rotating line

The gate and the footer already say 21+ and 1-800-GAMBLER. Leave those where they are. Do not repeat them as filler on the notepad or in a pitch.

Write the reason to come back. A line that only hedges the pitch gets deleted.

A notepad line is something a person would say out loud. It is a reason to show up or come back tomorrow.

Do not write feature labels, warnings, or product specs. These are bad:

- "Big payouts lose more often."
- "Look at the chance, not the juice."
- "I leave the tiny payouts off."
- "This week's picks are on different days."

Say what the person gets. "Tonight is handled." "Tomorrow I pick again." "The group chat is guessing."
